<task id="149" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>C10 part 2 (sharees) — internal users shared on a secure parent see exactly its children once the children are owned by the memberless secure team: verify Dataverse cascading share live first; otherwise the BFF mirrors the parent's share set onto each child at create and fans out on share/unshare — never wider than the parent</title>
    <phase>Register-driven (authored 2026-09-30, session 27; defect C10 half 2, owner round 2 item 6 "internal sharees' access to children")</phase>
    <gate>after 144, 145 and 146 are merged. Part A (live cascade verification) is startable as soon as 144 and 145 are live in dev. SHIP-TOGETHER partner of task 146 (146 must not reach a shared environment without this).</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Authorization .cs change on the POA share path (tags bff-api, auth, security) plus a possible Dataverse relationship-schema change; live verification gate.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security design with two mutually exclusive mechanisms (platform cascade vs BFF fan-out) chosen from live evidence; the failure modes are silent over-share (a child visible to someone not shared on the parent) and silent under-share (sharees lose their children).</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Modifies InternalShareEndpoints.cs, ProvisionProjectEndpoint.cs and UnsecureProjectEndpoint.cs (also edited by 139/142/143/144/148/150) and the owner hook installed by 146; 148 and 147 consume this task's synchronizer. Serialize with each; whichever runs second rebases.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>144, 145, 146</deps>
